518 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 285 0 R
/E (Reflection: Reflecting on this activity, it was beneficial for our team to follow the structured roles to be able to conduct the interviews and get instant qualitative feedback about the user experience of the app. Our results were, however, only applicable to members of the internal group, and therefore subject to peer response bias. Further, since we didn't use formal consent documentation because we were working within our team, it is good practice to have formal consent documentation for standardized research.  )
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
519 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 285 0 R
/E ( Beyond the activities in this section, in future iterations of the project we would like to recommend having a larger number of participants, including external and neutral shoppers, to get a wider user perspective. We would also do structured, task based usability testing like asking people to do things such as "Find the product" or "Use the coupon code" instead of "browse. Finally, we would ask for formal written consent before taking recordings and monitor quantitative data such as task completion time, navigation errors, etc., in addition to qualitative data such as feedback.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
